_pdbx_entry_details.entry_id             3QZ1 
_pdbx_entry_details.nonpolymer_details   
;THE LIGAND 3QZ IN THE STRUCTURE IS 17-HYDROXYPROGESTERONE, WHICH IS VERY HYDROPHOBIC AND ITS SOLUBILITY IS POOR. THE AUTHORS COULD NOT ADD MORE LIGAND DURING CRYSTALLIZATION DUE TO THE POOR SOLUBILITY. THIS IS PROBABLY WHY THE LIGANDS (ESPECIALLY B502) SHOWED RELATIVELY HIGH REAL SPACE R VALUES. THE DISORDER IS ALSO ONE OF THE REASON TO BE CONSIDERED. THERE ARE FOUR MOLECULES IN ASYMMETRIC UNIT. THREE OF FOUR MOLECULES A, C, AND D CLEARLY SHOWED TWO MOLECULES IN THE ENZYME. MOLECULE B SHOWED TWO MOLECULES AS WELL EVEN THOUGH B502 IS MORE DISORDERED SOMEHOW. IN ADDITION, THE BIOCHEMICAL TITRATION DATA PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE TO SUPPORT TWO LIGANDS BOUND IN THE ENZYME AT SAME TIME
;
